name: minimalist-ui
description: Clean editorial-style interfaces. Warm monochrome palette, typographic contrast, flat bento grids, muted pastels. No gradients, no heavy shadows.

# Minimalist UI Skill

## Overview
A premium utilitarian minimalism protocol for generating highly refined, ultra-minimalist, document-style web interfaces. Enforces high-contrast warm monochrome palettes, bespoke typographic hierarchies, and meticulous structural macro-whitespace.

## Key Features
- **Warm Monochrome Palette**: Canvas (#FFFFFF/#F7F6F3), surface (#FFFFFF/#F9F9F8), borders (#EAEAEA)
- **Editorial Typography**: Serif for headings, clean sans for body, mono for code
- **Bento Grid Layouts**: Asymmetrical CSS Grid with 1px borders and generous padding
- **Muted Pastel Accents**: Pale red, blue, green, yellow for tags and badges
- **Ultra-Flat Components**: No heavy shadows, no gradients, no glassmorphism

## Banned Elements
- Inter, Roboto, Open Sans fonts
- Lucide/Feather/Heroicons (use Phosphor Bold or Radix UI)
- Tailwind default shadows (shadow-md/lg/xl)
- Gradient, neon colors, glassmorphism
- Rounded-full for containers/cards/primary buttons
- Emojis anywhere

## Typography Architecture
- Sans-serif: SF Pro Display, Geist Sans, Switzer
- Editorial Serif: Lyon Text, Newsreader, Playfair Display
- Monospace: Geist Mono, SF Mono, JetBrains Mono
- Text colors: off-black #111111, muted #787774

## When to Use
- Editorial and publication-style websites
- Clean SaaS dashboards and admin panels
- Portfolio sites needing restrained elegance
- Any project where "less is more" applies

## Subtle Motion Guidelines
- Scroll entry: translateY(12px) + opacity over 600ms
- Hover: subtle shadow shift, scale(0.98) on active
- Staggered reveals with cascade delays
- Background ambient motion (slow radial gradient blobs)

